This product includes software developed at Anthropic PBC
(https://github.com/anthropics/claude-for-legal).

The review workflow, claim-classification block format, citation-confidence
tiering ([settled] / [verify] / [verify-pinpoint]), the "no silent supplement"
rule, and the non-lawyer approval gate in
device-claims/skills/device-claims-review/SKILL.md are derived from
product-legal/skills/marketing-claims-review/SKILL.md in
anthropics/claude-for-legal, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

Changes made: the US advertising-law substrate (FTC Act, NAD, state UDAP,
16 CFR Part 255) was removed in full and replaced with EU medical device
advertising law (MDR Art. 7, IVDR Art. 7) and German law (HWG, UWG).
The claim taxonomy was rebuilt around the four MDR Art. 7 limbs rather than
the generic puffery/factual/comparative/implied/absolute split.
